{"case_id":"T5035","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["API protocol","state","configuration","attack surface"],"commit_induced":"YES","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["spng_set_option","spng_get_option","require_bytes","write_data"],"reason":"S1 adds the public `SPNG_ENCODE_TO_BUFFER` option and a new encoding destination/state protocol, but H0 exercises only PNG input and decoding. It never selects the option, uses an encode-only context, or reaches the affected output-writing behavior. This gap is commit-induced because `SPNG_ENCODE_TO_BUFFER` and `ctx->internal_buffer` do not exist in S0.","evidence":["`spng_set_option()` adds `case SPNG_ENCODE_TO_BUFFER`, requires `ctx->encode_only`, rejects `ctx->state >= SPNG_STATE_OUTPUT`, and sets both `ctx->internal_buffer` and `ctx->state = SPNG_STATE_OUTPUT`.","`require_bytes()` newly returns `SPNG_ENODST` when `!ctx->internal_buffer`, and `write_data()` now propagates that specific return through `encode_err(ctx, ret)`.","`spng_get_option()` newly exposes the `ctx->internal_buffer` state through `SPNG_ENCODE_TO_BUFFER`.","H0 creates `spng_ctx_new(SPNG_CTX_IGNORE_ADLER32)`, configures input with `spng_set_png_file`, `spng_set_png_stream`, or `spng_set_png_buffer`, and calls decoding APIs such as `spng_decoded_image_size`, `spng_decode_image`, and `spng_decode_row`; it contains no encoding setup or `spng_set_option()` call.","The S0 declaration context has no matching declaration, while S1 adds `SPNG_ENCODE_TO_BUFFER` to `enum spng_option`."],"recommended_action":"Extend the fuzz harness with an encoding mode that creates an encode-only context, fuzzes `spng_set_option(ctx, SPNG_ENCODE_TO_BUFFER, value)` across valid and invalid values and state transitions, queries it with `spng_get_option()`, and drives encoding far enough to exercise `require_bytes()` and `write_data()` with and without an output destination."}
